 "text": "Hey, how's life treating you? That's very common. There's a reason people say a short walk or quick chat with a friend at lunch helps focus. So when you feel the guilt, is there one short break you could give yourself? Stand up, stretch, and do something different from what you were doing. Change of light, noise, or temperature can help. Exactly. A quick look is fine, but try not to make it the main activity. And don't beat yourself up if you end up working through the break. Maybe a short walk or quick lunch that takes less than half an hour. Set a timer so you' not in office forever.",
